---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import NeedHelp from '../../components/sections/NeedHelp.astro'
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../../components/seo/BreadcrumbSchema.astro'
import BlogPostingSchema from '../../components/seo/BlogPostingSchema.astro'
import FAQSchema from '../../components/seo/FAQSchema.astro'
import { seoData } from '../../lib/seo'

const seo = seoData.tamarindoVsJaco

const categories = [
  {
    category: 'Waves for Beginners',
    tamarindo: { score: 5, text: 'Slow, gentle beach break. Ideal for first-timers year-round. Waves are forgiving and readable.' },
    jaco: { score: 3, text: 'Faster, more powerful beach break. Great for intermediates but can be overwhelming for absolute beginners.' },
  },
  {
    category: 'Water Safety',
    tamarindo: { score: 5, text: 'Generally calm with predictable conditions. Riptides are manageable and well-marked. Certified instructors always present.' },
    jaco: { score: 3, text: 'Stronger currents and more powerful shorebreak. Requires more ocean awareness.' },
  },
  {
    category: 'Surf Schools',
    tamarindo: { score: 5, text: 'Multiple certified surf schools with professional instructors. Well-organized lesson programs for all levels.' },
    jaco: { score: 4, text: 'Good surf school scene, but more variable in quality. Do your research before booking.' },
  },
  {
    category: 'Town Vibe',
    tamarindo: { score: 4, text: 'International, surf-focused, relaxed. Great restaurants, cafÃ©s, nightlife. A little touristy but authentic.' },
    jaco: { score: 3, text: 'More party-oriented. Lively nightlife but can feel less family-friendly. Closer to San JosÃ©.' },
  },
  {
    category: 'Crowds',
    tamarindo: { score: 3, text: 'Popular spot â€” lineup can get crowded in peak season (Decâ€“Apr). Book lessons early.' },
    jaco: { score: 3, text: 'Similarly crowded during high season. Weekend warriors from San JosÃ© fill the lineup on Saturdays.' },
  },
  {
    category: 'Getting There',
    tamarindo: { score: 3, text: '4â€“5 hours from San JosÃ©. Worth the drive â€” or fly into Liberia for a 1.5-hour transfer.' },
    jaco: { score: 5, text: 'Only 1.5â€“2 hours from San JosÃ©. Easy day trip. The closest surf beach to the capital.' },
  },
]

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is Tamarindo or JacÃ³ better for learning to surf?', a: 'Tamarindo is better for beginners. The waves are slower and more forgiving, the surf school scene is more professional, and the overall environment is calmer and safer for first-timers.' },
  { q: 'Which is closer to San JosÃ© â€” Tamarindo or JacÃ³?', a: 'JacÃ³ is much closer â€” about 1.5â€“2 hours from San JosÃ©. Tamarindo is 4â€“5 hours away. If you only have a day trip, JacÃ³ is the easier choice.' },
  { q: 'Is Tamarindo safe for families?', a: 'Yes. Tamarindo is one of the most family-friendly surf destinations in Costa Rica. The beach is calm, the town is safe, and there are certified instructors experienced in teaching children.' },
  { q: 'What level is JacÃ³ surf?', a: 'JacÃ³ is best suited for intermediate and advanced surfers. The waves are faster and more powerful than Tamarindo. Beginners can still learn there, but expect a steeper learning curve.' },
  { q: 'Are there other surf spots worth considering near Tamarindo?', a: 'Yes. Within 30 minutes of Tamarindo you have Playa Avellanas, Playa Negra, and Playa Grande â€” all excellent surf spots with different wave types suited to different levels.' },
]
---

<BaseLayout title={seo.title} description={seo.description} slug={seo.slug} keyfocus={seo.keyfocus} image={seo.image} synonyms={seo.synonyms} type="article">
  <BreadcrumbSchema slot="head" items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'Blog',href:'/blog'},{name:'Tamarindo vs JacÃ³',href:seo.slug}]} />
  <BlogPostingSchema slot="head" title={seo.title} description={seo.description} slug={seo.slug} datePublished="2026-05-06" image="/images/surf-school-tamarindo-students.webp" authorName="Victor NuÃ±ez" />
  <FAQSchema slot="head" items={faqs.map(f => ({ question: f.q, answer: f.a }))} />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="bg-gray-900 py-20 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-20" style="background-image: url('/images/surf-school-tamarindo-students.webp'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-900/70 to-gray-900/95"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 container mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
          <a href="/blog" class="text-[#4DD0E1] text-sm font-semibold hover:underline">â† Blog</a>
          <span class="text-white/30">Â·</span>
          <span class="bg-purple-500/20 text-purple-300 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-purple-500/30">Destination Guide</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white mb-5 leading-tight">
          Tamarindo vs JacÃ³ for Beginner Surfers
        </h1>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Two of Costa Rica's most popular surf beaches. One is ideal for first-timers â€” the other is better once you already know what you're doing. Here's the honest comparison.
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-6 text-sm text-white/50">
          <span>May 6, 2026</span>
          <span>Â·</span>
          <span>6 min read</span>
          <span>Â·</span>
          <span>By Victor NuÃ±ez</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <article class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Costa Rica has world-class surf all along both coasts. But if you're a beginner trying to decide where to learn, the choice comes down to two main contenders: <strong>Tamarindo</strong> on the Pacific North and <strong>JacÃ³</strong> on the Central Pacific. Both are popular, both have surf schools â€” but they are not the same experience.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          At <a href="/best-surf-school-in-tamarindo" class="text-[#00BCD4] hover:underline">Pura Vida Surf School</a>, we teach hundreds of first-timers every year, and we get this question constantly. Here's our honest side-by-side breakdown â€” no fluff, just what actually matters when you're learning to surf.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- COMPARISON TABLE -->
  <section class="pb-16 bg-white">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-10 text-center">Head-to-Head Comparison</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          {categories.map(cat => (
            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
              <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-3">
                <h3 class="text-white font-bold text-sm">{cat.category}</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 divide-y md:divide-y-0 md:divide-x divide-gray-100">
                <div class="p-5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                    <span class="text-sm font-extrabold text-[#00BCD4]">Tamarindo</span>
                    <div class="flex gap-0.5">
                      {Array.from({length: 5}).map((_, i) => (
                        <svg class={`w-3 h-3 ${i < cat.tamarindo.score ? 'text-[#00BCD4]' : 'text-gray-200'}`} fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                          <path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z"/>
                        </svg>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{cat.tamarindo.text}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="p-5">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                    <span class="text-sm font-extrabold text-gray-500">JacÃ³</span>
                    <div class="flex gap-0.5">
                      {Array.from({length: 5}).map((_, i) => (
                        <svg class={`w-3 h-3 ${i < cat.jaco.score ? 'text-gray-400' : 'text-gray-200'}`} fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                          <path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z"/>
                        </svg>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{cat.jaco.text}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VERDICT -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-6">Our Verdict</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          <strong>For beginners, Tamarindo wins â€” and it's not even close.</strong> The waves are slower, more consistent, and more forgiving. You'll spend more time actually surfing and less time wiping out in heavy shore break. The surf school infrastructure is more developed, and the overall environment is more suited to learning at your own pace.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          JacÃ³ has a lot going for it â€” proximity to San JosÃ© being the biggest advantage. If you're only visiting for a weekend and can't make the drive to Tamarindo, JacÃ³ is a perfectly valid option. But if you're planning a dedicated surf trip and want to maximize your learning, make the extra effort to get to Tamarindo.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Once you're comfortable standing up and riding waves on your own â€” <em>then</em> JacÃ³'s more powerful waves become an asset for your progression.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-[#00BCD4]/8 border border-[#00BCD4]/20 rounded-3xl p-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Ready to Learn in Tamarindo?</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 mb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            We offer <a href="/private-surf-lessons-tamarindo" class="text-[#00BCD4] hover:underline">private lessons</a>, <a href="/group-surf-lessons-tamarindo" class="text-[#00BCD4] hover:underline">group lessons</a>, and <a href="/surf-camp-tamarindo" class="text-[#00BCD4] hover:underline">surf camps</a> for all levels. Certified instructors, all equipment included.
          </p>
          <a href="/book-now" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-[#00BCD4] text-white font-bold rounded-xl hover:bg-[#00ACC1] transition-colors text-sm">
            Book Your Lesson in Tamarindo
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
